---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { links } from '../config/links';

const title = 'Organisational partners';
const lead =
  'Membership of the Society is individual. Organisations that want to support it do so as partners.';
---

<Page title={title} eyebrow="Support" lead={lead}>
  <p class="lead">
    Organisations that want to support the Society can do so through sponsorship, event
    partnerships, venue support or commissioned activities.
  </p>

  <h2>What partnership does not buy</h2>
  <p>
    Financial or in-kind support does not purchase control over the Society's technical positions.
    Partnership arrangements will be transparent and consistent with the Society's sponsorship and
    partnership policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    This matters for a professional body whose value rests on the independence of its technical work.
    Partners are acknowledged; they do not set the agenda.
  </p>

  <h2>Ways to support the Society</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sponsorship</strong> — general support for the Society's programme.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Event partnership</strong> — supporting a seminar, workshop or the inaugural
      conference.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Venue support</strong> — hosting an in-person event.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Commissioned activities</strong> — work the Society undertakes at an organisation's
      request, on terms consistent with its independence.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Supporting your people</h2>
  <p>
    Many organisations support their staff's professional development directly, by meeting the cost
    of individual memberships and by making time available for the Society's programme. Members join
    in their own right, which is what allows them to take part in professional discussion without
    every contribution being read as their employer's position.
  </p>

  <Callout title="Sponsorship and partnership policy">
    <p>
      The Society's sponsorship and partnership policy is in preparation and will be published
      alongside its other governance documents.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    <Cta href={links.partnership} variant="primary">Enquire about partnership</Cta>
  </p>
</Page>
